  body: "# Net employed earnings for JSA and Income Support\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured
    passage defines net earnings as gross earnings less specified income-tax, Class 1 contribution and
    pension-contribution deductions.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThis does not mean every payroll deduction
    or expense is allowable. Pension period alignment and qualifying scheme rules are separate, and current
    law and applicable benefit must be verified. No deduction amount or award is calculated here; the
    source wording remains available for review.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 26020, PDF
    page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f9ba20b52e4144868938/dmg-Ch-26.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 26: Employed earners.\n- [DMG 26027, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f9ba20b52e4144868938/dmg-Ch-26.pdf#page=10)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 26: Employed earners.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch26`: PDF SHA-256 `fe619693d2f8cc78cac3786dadab88e81467ec56d38f00727285612af92b80c9`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `f4089f7088e6a987d028072f4968eb39f2686b7a588e2c38f8ebc1cb3042102a`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-employed-earner
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The net-earnings passage belongs to the employed-earner treatment and must be read
      with its employment definition rather than the separate self-employment profit method.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch26/0005
      quote: "26010 The term employed earner means1 a person who is gainfully employed in GB\n\n\n1. under
        a contract of service or\n\n\n2. in an office (including an elective office) with general earnings
        2.\n\n\n                                             1 JSA Regs, reg 3; IS (Gen) Regs, reg 2(1);
        SS CB Act 92, s 2(1)(a);\n                                                      2 Income Tax (Earnings
        and Pensions) Act 2003, s 7(3)"
      locator: DMG 26010
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch26/0009
      quote: "26020 Net earnings are gross earnings less1\n\n\n1. income tax and\n\n\n2. Class 1 SS contributions
        and\n\n\n3. half of any sum paid by the employee, towards an occupational or personal pension
        scheme.\n\n\n                                                          1 JSA Regs, reg 99(4);
        IS (Gen) Regs, reg 36(3)"
      locator: DMG 26020
